 The list of discovered PuppetDB targets is refreshed at the interval, which can be configured via `-promscrape.puppetdbSDCheckInterval` command-line flag.
 
+## scaleway_sd_configs
+
+Scaleway SD configuration discovers scrape targets from [Scaleway](https://www.scaleway.com/en/) Instances.
+
+Configuration example:
+
+```yaml
+scrape_configs:
+- job_name: scaleway
+  scaleway_sd_configs:
+
+    # project_id or organization_id must be set to the id of the Scaleway Project
+    # or Organization to discover Instances from.
+  - project_id: "..."
+
+    # secret_key is the Scaleway API secret key to send as `X-Auth-Token`
+    # in every HTTP API request during service discovery (mandatory).
+    # See: https://www.scaleway.com/en/docs/identity-and-access-management/iam/how-to/create-api-keys/
+    secret_key: "..."
+
+    # zone is an optional Scaleway zone, e.g. `fr-par-1`, to limit service discovery to.
+    # By default, Instances are discovered across all the known Scaleway zones.
+    #
+    # zone: "fr-par-1"
+
+    # api_url is an optional URL of the Scaleway API server.
+    # By default, https://api.scaleway.com is used.
+    #
+    # api_url: "..."
+
+    # Scaleway provides query arguments to filter instances.
+    # See: https://www.scaleway.com/en/developers/api/instance/#path-servers-list-all-servers
+
+    # name_filter is an optional query argument to filter instances by name.
+    #
+    # name_filter: "..."
+
+    # tags_filter is an optional list of tags to filter instances by.
+    #
+    # tags_filter: ["...", "..."]
+
+    # port is an optional port to scrape metrics from.
+    # By default, port 80 is used.
+    #
+    # port: ...
+
+    # Additional HTTP API client options can be specified here.
+    # See https://docs.victoriametrics.com/victoriametrics/sd_configs/#http-api-client-options
+```
+
+Each discovered target has an [`__address__`](https://docs.victoriametrics.com/victoriametrics/relabeling/#how-to-modify-scrape-urls-in-targets) label set
+to `<IP>:<port>`, where `<IP>` is the discovered instance's public IPv4 address (or, when it has none, its private IPv4 address), and `<port>` is the port
+from the `scaleway_sd_configs` (default port is `80`). Only Instances in the `running` state are discovered.
+
+The following meta labels are available on discovered targets during [relabeling](https://docs.victoriametrics.com/victoriametrics/relabeling/):
+
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_arch`: the architecture of the instance, such as `x86_64` or `arm64`.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_boot_type`: the boot type used by the instance.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_hostname`: the hostname of the instance.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_id`: the unique ID of the instance.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_name`: the name of the instance.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_organization_id`: the ID of the organization the instance belongs to.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_private_ipv4`: the private IPv4 address of the instance.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_project_id`: the ID of the project the instance belongs to.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_public_ipv4`: the public IPv4 address of the instance, if any.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_public_ipv6`: the public IPv6 address of the instance, if any.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_security_group_id`: the ID of the security group the instance belongs to.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_security_group_name`: the name of the security group the instance belongs to.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_state`: the state of the instance.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_tags`: comma-separated list of tags applied to the instance.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_type`: the commercial type (instance type) of the instance.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_zone`: the zone the instance is located in, e.g. `fr-par-1`.
+
+The list of discovered Scaleway targets is refreshed at the interval, which can be configured via `-promscrape.scalewaySDCheckInterval` command-line flag.
+
 ## static_configs
 
 A static config allows specifying a list of targets and a common label set for them.
